%% The investigation case state machine.
%%
%% Defined in backend/app/services/case_state_machine.py and tested
%% exhaustively in backend/tests/test_case_transitions.py: every ordered pair
%% of states, not just the legal ones.
%%
%% What each transition requires is the part that matters. They are not
%% decoration: closing without a disposition is the single most expensive
%% omission in the workflow, because every later measurement of detection
%% quality reads that field and it cannot be reconstructed afterwards.

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> NEW

    NEW --> TRIAGED: triage<br/>(assignment does this)
    NEW --> UNDER_INVESTIGATION: start<br/>needs an assignee
    NEW --> CLOSED: close<br/>needs a disposition

    TRIAGED --> UNDER_INVESTIGATION: start<br/>needs an assignee
    TRIAGED --> ESCALATED: escalate<br/>needs a reason
    TRIAGED --> CLOSED: close<br/>needs a disposition

    UNDER_INVESTIGATION --> ESCALATED: escalate<br/>needs a reason
    UNDER_INVESTIGATION --> CLOSED: close<br/>needs a disposition

    ESCALATED --> UNDER_INVESTIGATION: de_escalate<br/>needs a reason
    ESCALATED --> CLOSED: close<br/>needs a disposition

    CLOSED --> UNDER_INVESTIGATION: reopen<br/>needs a reason

    note right of UNDER_INVESTIGATION
        Needs an owner. A case here
        that nobody owns counts as
        active everywhere and has
        nobody accountable for it.
    end note

    note right of CLOSED
        Not terminal -- new information
        arrives. Reopens to
        UNDER_INVESTIGATION, never to
        NEW: the work already recorded
        is part of the case.
    end note
